{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"B7JB87","uniProtkbId":"ATPD_ACIF2","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2009-07-28","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2009-02-10","entryVersion":79,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":2.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Acidithiobacillus ferrooxidans (strain ATCC 23270 / DSM 14882 / CIP 104768 / NCIMB 8455)","commonName":"Ferrobacillus ferrooxidans (strain ATCC 23270)","taxonId":243159,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Acidithiobacillia","Acidithiobacillales","Acidithiobacillaceae","Acidithiobacillus"]},"proteinExistence":"3: Inferred from homology","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"ATP synthase subunit delta"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"ATP synthase F(1) sector subunit delta"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"F-type ATPase subunit delta"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"F-ATPase subunit delta"}]}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"atpH"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"AFE_3206"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"F(1)F(0) ATP synthase produces ATP from ADP in the presence of a proton or sodium gradient. F-type ATPases consist of two structural domains, F(1) containing the extramembraneous catalytic core and F(0) containing the membrane proton channel, linked together by a central stalk and a peripheral stalk. During catalysis, ATP synthesis in the catalytic domain of F(1) is coupled via a rotary mechanism of the central stalk subunits to proton translocation"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"This protein is part of the stalk that links CF(0) to CF(1). It either transmits conformational changes from CF(0) to CF(1) or is implicated in proton conduction"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"F-type ATPases have 2 components, F(1) - the catalytic core - and F(0) - the membrane proton channel. F(1) has five subunits: alpha(3), beta(3), gamma(1), delta(1), epsilon(1). F(0) has three main subunits: a(1), b(2) and c(10-14). The alpha and beta chains form an alternating ring which encloses part of the gamma chain. F(1) is attached to F(0) by a central stalk formed by the gamma and epsilon chains, while a peripheral stalk is formed by the delta and b chains"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"Cell inner membrane","id":"SL-0037"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"Peripheral membrane protein","id":"SL-9903"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01416"}],"value":"Belongs to the ATPase delta chain family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":179,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"ATP synthase subunit delta","featureId":"PRO_1000184633"}],"keywords":[{"id":"KW-0066","category":"Biological process","name":"ATP synthesis"},{"id":"KW-0997","category":"Cellular component","name":"Cell inner membrane"},{"id":"KW-1003","category":"Cellular component","name":"Cell membrane"},{"id":"KW-0139","category":"Cellular component","name":"CF(1)"},{"id":"KW-0375","category":"Biol